'''''Groenlandia''''' is a [[monotypic]] [[genus]] of [[aquatic plant]]s (pondweed) of the family [[Potamogetonaceae]]. The only species in the genus is '''''Groenlandia densa'''''.<ref name="Wilkins">{{cite book|last1=Les|first1=Donald H.|last2 = Tippery|first2 = Nicholas P.|title=Early Events in Monocot Evolution|editor=Paul Wilkins and Simon J. Mayo|publisher=Cambridge University Press|date=2013|pages=118–164|chapter=In time and with water...the systematics of alismatid monocotyledons}}</ref> '''Opposite-leaved pondweed''' is a common name for this plant.<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> It is native to much of Europe, western Asia and [[Maghreb]] in Africa; despite its name it is not found in Greenland.<ref name="iucn status 11 November 2021" />

